{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>When men strive together</b> כי ינצו is juxtaposed to חלוץ הנעל (removal of the shoe), for through halitzah strife comes, as we say: once there are sons for your sons, peace is upon Israel, for he is exempt from halitzah and yibum." "<b>And she seizes</b> — two times in the Masorah: this one, and the other והחזיקה בו ונשקה לו (and she seized him and kissed him). העיזה פניה (she brazened her face) — only if she seized intentionally, as written העיזה פניה ותאמר לו (she brazened her face and said to him); but if unwittingly, she is exempt."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:40.729873071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}